{"type":"message","id":"cc94a636","parentId":"786fd85b","timestamp":"2026-03-18T16:45:32.379Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_00fd6c95bd007ad00169bad6a5a1dc81918287f56929e46698\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABputamr8kFd7sH00qcHLknMhTMbE8daiJZEaI4Qv213m9oACdJzQFWI_yqpD37VntOvDNmhyMfEvnvVbV6pNRhoJWQIV-lfsLwsbFJboXLw0Dwr13XLJsYt2sp5mdxswtvBIQCOZTuba0ebKiLA4_mRYTUxQNgjAOrJuSPf8y3loKH1uFSTQkIuzuNz2K47N5U9ki_BUZFfjpPiYT2ZagSyi-2N32AeWU3fX7nJIhyrpkj96gPIYp7KEWcMLaf8zQl1mKfKLXvbc9R8H_L50Um2PafPYmN3SLOynaoeSk6GjNiksoJtUppGLiApUN11cWdNMcQLB1Ed-nY5VVqTnvMITQ1q9NjP3uFUCXY_1ieZgv7VqJ6kwWNnvZ30UGHMUl5yp446yXHKNv7hnnAJqBSbkvSwvPbiI55zrJc9sAs7tbN9AIAl8YRkGom2UGHryUVpKYGnZUxBuxFBlfS-DOVtLaqpmkzhE7Ichw-hwEqugvi6rcBcPnIaXsn0OEYm19tIom1Vj_a3wCDv0K75Ky0fSe_aRZAA0zybBO88Xb6xlGJhG21rcaH5c0jAJpW9R5zQFflV9DC8YMiLt2KAGmyksQjx9Gid9Z_hQSwDzN2p9XYxcmuvDnIVJTrzjyWnFt3vg2BD26INqsB2pNXY6LhueAPKXdKaIXYWhQq_oUm3ilbdEl_vD44ASz7VQKV73T0umijnXStKbndCXsc77AEyLhqzcTf2KYbuS2xpRIaKHMh0KT196cPM7K__VVl0pqmMgVYCYzK3SDHlg1XNh6HOZZwItixIosDzFzAKkuCxziWqed28664q5OWYXJb5H8JMKWnxCgdekSZLbBy5vgVNzv43g==\",\"summary\":[]}"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] Yes — I checked it, and the script was already sending the **correct Telegram user id** to the upload endpoint.\n\nWhat’s happening is this:\n\n- **Telegram user id actually sent to upload endpoint:** `495506013`\n- **Upload request URL used:**  \n  `http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/nodes/input/upload?storage_ref=nodes_bucket&local_file_path=upload%2F&user_id=495506013`\n\nThe id you were seeing change or look unrelated is **not the Telegram id**. It’s a **backend/internal platform id** returned inside the pipeline/prototype response, for example:\n- `prototype_players[0].user_id = 626130f7c71f6b9e651c76be`\n\nThat internal id belongs to the prototype/backend system, not to Telegram.\n\n### Fix applied\nI updated the script **without changing the pipeline behavior** so future runs now explicitly expose:\n- `local_image_path_used`\n- `telegram_user_id_used_for_upload`\n- `upload_path`\n- `upload_filename`\n- `upload_request_url`\n- `raw_upload_response`\n\nSo now it’s easy to verify which Telegram id was actually used for upload, and to distinguish it from backend ids in the response.\n\n### Verified result from the test run\n- **Telegram user id used for upload:** `495506013`\n- **Returned upload path:** `upload/2026-03-18_16.45.46_MCUE4FVVVDltFGai6Xlt/`\n\nIf you want, I can do one more cleanup pass and make the user-facing summary **hide backend internal ids entirely**, so this confusion doesn’t show up again.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_00fd6c95bd007ad00169bad6a678f88191a19c9d18a5de204b\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":11209,"output":368,"cacheRead":37120,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":48697,"cost":{"input":0.028022500000000002,"output":0.00552,"cacheRead":0.00928,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0428225}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1773852324350}}
